changeme

# This is a Docker secret file, not a .env file: it must contain ONLY the
# raw SMTP password as its content (no KEY=VALUE syntax, no quotes).
#
# Setup:
#   cp secrets/smtp_password.example secrets/smtp_password
#   edit secrets/smtp_password to hold your real SMTP password (single line)
#   chmod 0644 secrets/smtp_password
#
# The 0644 permission is required because the container runs as a non-root
# user (uid 10001) that needs read access to the secret bind-mounted by
# Docker Compose at /run/secrets/smtp_password. secrets/smtp_password is
# already listed in .gitignore -- never commit your real password.
